VulkanFluid — GPU continuum liquid
  build.c                          static C++17 library
  fld/fld.hpp                      public API
  fld/continuum/continuum.hpp      user settings and render inputs
  fld/continuum/continuum.cpp      GPU allocations, dispatch, render integration
  fld/continuum/shaders/grid.comp  staggered MAC grid and volume-fraction solver
  fld/continuum/shaders/surface.comp  volume isosurface + full-resolution composite
  fld/material/                    SI material properties

The active backend no longer simulates a fluid as independent SPH spheres.
It stores liquid occupancy as a 3D cell-centered volume fraction (VOF), with
velocities on MAC grid faces. A pressure Poisson solve enforces approximate
incompressibility and a finite-volume face flux transports volume between
cells. Free surfaces can merge, break apart and interact with solid geometry.
The surface is raymarched from trilinearly interpolated VOF instead of per-
particle raymarching. Curvature provides a simple Laplace pressure boundary
condition, and a contact-angle approximation applies near horizontal solids.

The core solver is a FIRST CONTINUUM BASELINE, not a verified scientific
solver. Donor-cell upwind advection is first order and may diffuse interfaces.
Pressure uses 36 Jacobi iterations by default, not geometric multigrid and
not residual-based convergence. It may exhibit divergence error, contact-angle
error and volume loss under high Courant numbers or insufficient resolution.
The current implementation does not yet have APIC/FLIP, conservative PLIC
interface reconstruction, or a coupled shallow-water/thin-film specialization.
Do not claim those features are implemented.

The whole grid is allocated on the GPU. Default 64 x 40 x 64 at 10 cm cells.
Simulation and rendering run as ordered GPU compute passes; they cannot be
correctly collapsed into one dispatch because pressure iterations require
global synchronization. Timestep is capped to avoid obvious CFL violations.
Low frame rates slow simulated time rather than dropping liquid through the
floor. Control speed and physical resolution in the host's client.cpp.

API:
  fld::continuum::init(options,drop,shader_paths,frames,width,height)
  fld::continuum::record(command,frame_index,elapsed_seconds,render_input)
  fld::continuum::active()
  fld::continuum::shutdown()

VulkanEngine must be initialized first. The host provides renderer image views,
scene boxes, color and shader paths. Generic library knows no game-specific
weapons, characters or blood. Independent bvh/ library remains reusable; the
current continuum solver rasterizes a small collider set only once at startup.

Validation required on actual GPU:
  compile seven grid compute stages, volume render and upscaler;
  step test, gravity, pooled water, coalescence, volume measurement, divergence
  residual and collider boundaries; profile passes separately on M2.
60 FPS and physically accurate contact-line motion are not yet validated.
